# Valgrind suppressions for `make memcheck`.
#
# ctest -T memcheck wraps the command of every test, and for the shell-script tests (killloop,
# soiltools, soakcheck) that command is `sh script`, so Valgrind checks the shell itself.  dash
# leaks one 15-byte strdup at exit in all three; the stack never leaves dash.  Nothing of ours
# is involved, and every other leak (ours or another program's) still fails the run.
{
   dash-strdup-at-exit
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:strdup
   obj:*/dash
   ...
}
